  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p>NutritionFacts.org has so many free resources to help you on your journey to a healthier life.</p>\n<h2><b><i>The Evidence-Based Eating Guide</i></b></h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><i><br/>\nThe Evidence-Based Eating Guide: A Healthy Living Resource from Dr. Greger &amp; NutritionFacts.org</i> simplifies making the switch to a healthier lifestyle. It’s an easy-to-understand guide, bursting with information on eating more healthfully, including a breakdown of<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dining-by-traffic-light-green-is-for-go-red-is-for-stop/\"> Dr. Greger’s Traffic Light Eating</a>, tips for using his <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\">Daily Dozen Checklist</a>, sample menus, and more.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-103781\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"163\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo.png 599w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-540x855.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 163px) 100vw, 163px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">English</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-103783\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-es.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"163\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-es.png 600w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-es-540x857.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 163px) 100vw, 163px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/bp0ahfnzq6j2cx7n4t5i2u2vzbcx7iqz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spanish</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-103787\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-cn-1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"163\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-cn-1.png 600w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/eg-solo-cn-1-540x853.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 163px) 100vw, 163px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.box.com/v/cn-eating-guide\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chinese</a></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><b><i>Daily Dozen Meal Planning Guide</i></b></h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%; text-align: center;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%; text-align: center;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%; text-align: center;\"> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The healthiest diet is one that maximizes the intake of foods-as-grown—whole, plant-based foods—and minimizes the consumption of processed and animal-based foods. In the first half of his book,<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die/\"> <i>How Not to Die</i></a>, Dr. Greger covers the <i>whys</i> of eating healthfully, exploring diet’s role in the prevention, treatment, and sometimes even reversal of the fifteen leading causes of death in the United States. In the book’s second half, he dives into the <i>hows</i> of eating healthfully and shares his Daily Dozen checklist, grocery shopping tips, and meal planning ideas.</p>\n<p>In our <i>Daily Dozen Meal Planning Guide</i>, we walk you through the steps for incorporating the Daily Dozen checklist into your life and give you additional strategies to help you build more healthful eating habits. Download your free copy of the guide today!</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-103790 aligncenter\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"213\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo.jpg 851w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-768x932.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-720x874.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-540x655.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 213px) 100vw, 213px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">English</a></p>\n<p> </p></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-103792 aligncenter\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-es.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"213\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-es.jpg 851w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-es-768x931.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-es-720x873.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-es-540x655.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 213px) 100vw, 213px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/ke4bmadzuc6t74tr978rttp73lsf6sou\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spanish</a></p>\n<p> </p></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-103794 aligncenter\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-cn.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"213\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-cn.jpg 851w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-cn-768x931.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-cn-720x873.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/mpg-solo-cn-540x655.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 213px) 100vw, 213px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.box.com/file/1350765445946?s=sh5eivtjzs1tnsflox8wnvfxlr2hi8tn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chinese</a></p>\n<p> </p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><b>Infographics</b></h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\">\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103815\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/dd-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"185\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/dd-1.jpg 746w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/dd-1-720x1003.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/dd-1-540x752.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 185px) 100vw, 185px\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/7iqjel4ymt2mc5ab9ztkd4yjg04j8421\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Daily Dozen</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103817\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/vit-d.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"196\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/vit-d.jpg 792w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/vit-d-768x1010.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/vit-d-720x947.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/vit-d-540x710.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 196px) 100vw, 196px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/sj5ux3jff0r726x5x0e48sf8h0dx0ih6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vitamin D</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103819\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/b12-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"191\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/b12-1.jpg 774w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/b12-1-768x1036.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/b12-1-720x971.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/b12-1-540x728.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 191px) 100vw, 191px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/j3w6zg5kjcf6vkgoy69i7i48zhe5i62u\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vitamin B12</a></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103821\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/plant-based-meat.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"233\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/plant-based-meat.jpg 942w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/plant-based-meat-768x850.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/plant-based-meat-720x796.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/plant-based-meat-540x597.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 233px) 100vw, 233px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/mju0o48ofqm1snag2ibiqiszri4v8wl2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Meat Alternatives</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-103823 aligncenter\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fasting.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"221\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fasting.jpg 893w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fasting-768x895.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fasting-720x839.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fasting-540x629.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 221px) 100vw, 221px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/qohie4mzesf4w99etg7qcnxqce3jrduo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fasting</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103825\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/sweet-potatoes.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/sweet-potatoes.jpg 808w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/sweet-potatoes-768x989.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/sweet-potatoes-720x927.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/sweet-potatoes-540x695.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/s/rbkej9evdfisnyiqil47y85zaej8e892\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sweet Potatoes</a></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-103827 aligncenter\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/aa8-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"203\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/aa8-1.jpg 822w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/aa8-1-768x974.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/aa8-1-720x914.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/aa8-1-540x685.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 203px) 100vw, 203px\"/><p></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.box.com/v/anti-aging-eight\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Anti-Aging</a></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Interested in <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.box.com/v/spanish-infographics\">Spanish infographics</a>?</p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Email Series</b></h2>\n<p>We offer three great email series to support you in living healthfully:</p>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">Join us for our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/how-to-live-longer/\">How to Live Longer series</a>, where we go through some of the most important information Dr. Greger uncovered on the science behind healthy aging. <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/how-to-live-longer/\">Sign up</a> for this email series and learn how to live longer, vibrantly. </li>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">Our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/plantbased-living-series/\">Plant-Based Living weekly email series</a> gives you simplified takeaways and actionable tips on healthy eating. Whether you’re new to a whole food, plant-based lifestyle or would benefit from reminders on some of the key aspects of evidence-based nutrition, this series is for you.</li>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">Join us for <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/daily-dozen/\">11 weeks of Daily Dozen support emails</a> to help you <i>Do the Dozen</i> with ease.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Optimum Nutrient Recommendations</b></h2>\n<p>Check out our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/optimum-nutrient-recommendations/\">Optimum Nutrient Recommendations</a> for more on vitamin B12, calcium, vitamin D, omega-3 fatty acids, iodine, iron, and selenium. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Topic Pages</b></h2>\n<p>To view all of our videos organized by topic, explore our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/\">topic pages</a>. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Recipes</b></h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/sweet-potato-taquitos/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-103723\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/potato-taquitos-2-720x720-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"720\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/potato-taquitos-2-720x720-1.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/potato-taquitos-2-720x720-1-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/potato-taquitos-2-720x720-1-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\"/></a></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/fruit-and-nut-bars/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-103719\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fruit-and-nut-bars-7-720x720-1.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"720\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fruit-and-nut-bars-7-720x720-1.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fruit-and-nut-bars-7-720x720-1-500x500.jpeg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/fruit-and-nut-bars-7-720x720-1-540x540.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\"/></a></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/hearty-veggie-soup/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-103721\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/hearty-veg-soup-14-720x720-1.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"720\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/hearty-veg-soup-14-720x720-1.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/hearty-veg-soup-14-720x720-1-500x500.jpeg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/hearty-veg-soup-14-720x720-1-540x540.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\"/></a></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/banana-oat-cookies/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-103717\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/banana-oat-cookies-2-720x720-1.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"720\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/banana-oat-cookies-2-720x720-1.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/banana-oat-cookies-2-720x720-1-500x500.jpeg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/banana-oat-cookies-2-720x720-1-540x540.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\"/></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Each <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipes/\">recipe in our collection</a> uses only health-promoting ingredients, based on Dr. Greger’s<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/daily-dozen/\"> Daily Dozen</a> and dining by<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dining-by-traffic-light-green-is-for-go-red-is-for-stop/\"> traffic light system</a>. These whole food, plant-based dishes, sauces, condiments, and sides come from<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die-cookbook/\"> <i>The How Not to Die Cookbook</i></a> and<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\"> <i>The How Not to Diet Cookbook</i></a>, part of Dr. Greger’s award-winning series, as well as contributions from the NutritionFacts.org team and friends.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"DONATE\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">VIEW ALL RECIPES</a></p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Dr. Greger’s Live Presentations</b></h2>\n<p>From the comfort of your own home, join Dr. Greger as he dives into the content of each of his acclaimed books with these recordings of his <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/annual-talks/\">live presentations</a>.</p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Podcast</b></h2>\n<p>Listen to the <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\">Nutrition Facts with Dr. Greger</a> podcast and take Dr. Greger with you in the car and on walks. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Live Q&amp;As</b></h2>\n<p>Join Dr. Greger live each month for an exciting Q&amp;A. <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\">Sign up</a> to our free newsletter to get the date and link directly in your inbox. You can also check out <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\">past Q&amp;A sessions</a> recordings.</p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Webinars </b></h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%;\">\n<p>A few times a year, Dr. Greger hosts <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinars/\">webinars</a> on a wide range of topics, such as <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/how-to-prevent-and-treat-age-related-hearing-loss/\">hearing loss</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/preventing-and-treating-osteoporosis/\">osteoporosis</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/should-you-supplement-with-vitamin-k2/\">vitamin K2</a>, and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/are-potassium-salt-substitutes-safe-and-effective/\">potassium salt substitutes</a>. Sign up for our free <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\">newsletter</a> to receive the latest webinar updates. Don’t miss the chance to sign up for our upcoming CME-approved webinar on May 10. </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-103830\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2024/05/cme.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"175\" height=\"175\"/></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><b>International Content </b></h2>\n<p>The entire <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/es/\">NutritionFacts.org</a> website has been translated into Spanish, and we also have Spanish <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFactsEspanol/\">Facebook</a> and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nutritionfactsespanol/\">Instagram</a> pages. On DrGreger.org, you’ll find <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/filter-spanish\">shirts</a>, <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/nutrition-nerd-kiss-cut-stickers-en-espanol\">stickers</a>, and <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/evidence-based-eating-guide-es\"><i>Evidence-Based Eating Guides</i></a> in Spanish.</p>\n<p>Check out our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/china/\">NutritionFacts in China</a> page for links to all our Chinese content, including social media, books, and infographics. On DrGreger.org, we also have <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/filter-chinese\">shirts</a> and <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/evidence-based-eating-guide-chinese\"><i>Evidence-Based Eating Guides</i></a> in Chinese.</p>\n<p>Dr. Greger’s books have been translated in many languages. Check out <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4406241003035-How-to-Order-Dr-Greger-s-Books\">this page</a> for more information. </p>\n<p>Want to see all the NutritionFacts videos available in your language? Visit our<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/?s=/\"> search page</a> and check out the <b>‘Subtitle Language</b>’ menu on the right side or press the <b>‘Filters</b>’ button if you’re on mobile. After you select your language, the results will list all the videos with subtitles available in that language. View this page for instructions on how to access subtitles and translations in our videos:<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/213775987-Viewing-closed-captions-and-translations\"> Closed Captions and Translations</a>.</p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Host a Screening</b></h2>\n<p>Share the latest in evidence-based nutrition with your community by hosting a <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/screenings/\">free screening</a> of Dr. Greger’s “<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\">How Not to Die</a>,” “<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\">Evidence-Based Weight Loss</a>,“ or “<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-age-live-presentation/\">How Not to Age</a>” presentation. Each video runs for approximately one hour. Your free Digital Event Kit will include the video, an introduction to NutritionFacts, a fun trivia game for attendees (not included in the “How Not to Age” screening kit), and tips for hosting. Each <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/screenings/\">screening event</a> is approximately two hours long.</p>\n<p>By providing this fun and educational event kit, we hope to make it easier than ever to spread the message about evidence-based eating.</p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Volunteer </b></h2>\n<p>If you are interested in volunteering with NutritionFacts.org, check out our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/\">open positions</a>. Also, please consider subscribing to our<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/nutritionmission/\"> Nutrition Mission Newsletter</a>. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>Speaking Tour </b></h2>\n<p>Want to see Dr. Greger in person and get your books signed? Check out his <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/speaking-dates/\">speaking tour calendar</a>. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>DrGreger.org </b></h2>\n<p><b><br/>\n</b>In the DrGreger.org store, you can find digital downloads of our <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/videos\">video collections</a>, <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch\">shirts</a>, and <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/filter-outreach\">outreach material</a>. The print versions of our <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/healthkit\">English</a>, <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/evidence-based-eating-guide-es\">Spanish</a>, and <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch/products/evidence-based-eating-guide-chinese\">Chinese</a> <i>Evidence-Based Eating Guides</i> are 20% off through May 20, 2024. </p>\n<p>If you missed Dr. Greger’s <i>How Not to Age</i> Book Club Webinar Series, the recording is available on <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/videos/products/how-not-to-age-book-club-digital\">DrGreger.org</a>. </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2><b>The Daily Dozen App</b></h2>\n<p>Download the free Daily Dozen app today and start including some of the healthiest foods in your diet. Track your servings, analyze your progress, and learn along the way. The app is available in the <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/dr-gregers-daily-dozen/id1060700802\">App Store</a> and <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.nutritionfacts.dailydozen\">Google Play</a>.</p>"
  }
